    {
      "title": "Isaias strengthens to become first Atlantic hurricane of 2026 season",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/09/isaias-strengthens-first-atlantic-hurricane-2026",
      "description": "<p>Storm expected to make landfall on US’s northern Gulf coast with risk of flash floods and isolated river flooding</p><p>Isaias has become the first Atlantic hurricane of the 2026 season, with wind speeds of 80mph and a minimum pressure of 975mb. It is expected to strengthen to a category 2 hurricane as it approaches the US’s northern Gulf coast on Friday, according to the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA).</p><p>As a result of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/26/what-is-el-nino-causes-can-we-reduce-risks\">the strong El Niño</a>, it has been a notably quiet Atlantic hurricane season. The first hurricane of the season has not formed this late since 8 October 1905, which pre-dates the satellite era (1960s) for tracking hurricanes that has allowed for more non-landfall hurricanes to be discovered.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/09/isaias-strengthens-first-atlantic-hurricane-2026\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-09T09:59:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Key things to know about Hurricane Isaias as millions under evacuation orders",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/global/2026/oct/09/hurricane-isaias-where-path-landfall-preparation",
      "description": "<p>The hurricane is first in the Atlantic in what has turned into a very late season. Here’s what forecasters are saying about where Isaias will hit and how hard</p><p>Hurricane Isaias, which made landfall on the US Gulf coast Friday night, was forecast to bring a dangerous storm surge, significant rainfall, flooding and strong winds across the US Gulf coast this weekend. Millions of people across several states, including Florida, Georgia and Alabama, were under evacuation orders as officials prepared for the storm. All three states issued states of emergency.</p><p>The hurricane, the first in the Atlantic in what has turned into a very late 2026 season, made landfall as a category 2 storm, with sustained winds of 105 mph.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/global/2026/oct/09/hurricane-isaias-where-path-landfall-preparation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-10T01:50:32"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hurricane Isaias makes landfall in Florida with severe effects expected across several states",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/hurricane-isaias-makes-landfall",
      "description": "<p>Governors of Mississippi, Alabama and Florida declared states of emergency as a downsized Fema faces first major test</p><p>Hurricane Isaias made landfall near Destin, Florida, on Friday evening, sweeping ashore from the northern Gulf of Mexico as the first Atlantic hurricane of the 2026 season.</p><p>The National Hurricane Center (NHC) in Miami said the center of the cyclone made landfall at 9.30pm ET as a category 2 hurricane with winds reaching 105 mph (165km/h).</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/hurricane-isaias-makes-landfall\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-10T01:44:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Life-threatening storm surge’ headed to US Gulf coast as residents brace for Isaias",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/hurricane-isaias-gulf-coast",
      "description": "<p>Alabama, Florida and Mississippi declare emergencies, with preparations under way for ‘long-duration power outages’</p><p>Hurricane Isaias neared landfall Friday evening, barreling toward the US Gulf coast coast as a dangerous category 2 storm and prompting emergency declarations in Alabama, Florida and Mississippi.</p><p>The hurricane, the first in the Atlantic in what has turned into a very late 2026 season, is expected to cause a “life-threatening storm surge”, officials said. Isaias is forecast to make landfall on Friday night, somewhere along the western Florida Panhandle, with surging seas up to about 7ft (2.1 meters) and waves as high as 30ft (9.1 meters).</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/hurricane-isaias-gulf-coast\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-10T00:18:15"
    },
    {
